\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The four backbones and the paired tests between AI-only and the hybrid. All backbones share the encoder (\texttt  {microsoft/mdeberta-v3-base}), tokenizer, split and evaluation code and differ only in the optimisation recipe. $\Delta =\text  {AI}-\text  {hybrid}$ in macro-F1, so a negative value favours the hybrid; the 95\% interval is the paired-bootstrap percentile interval over 10{,}000 resamples. $b$ is the number of comments the AI gets right and the hybrid gets wrong, $c$ the reverse; the last column is the exact McNemar $p$.}}{7}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:backbones}{{1}{7}{The four backbones and the paired tests between AI-only and the hybrid. All backbones share the encoder (\texttt {microsoft/mdeberta-v3-base}), tokenizer, split and evaluation code and differ only in the optimisation recipe. $\Delta =\text {AI}-\text {hybrid}$ in macro-F1, so a negative value favours the hybrid; the 95\% interval is the paired-bootstrap percentile interval over 10{,}000 resamples. $b$ is the number of comments the AI gets right and the hybrid gets wrong, $c$ the reverse; the last column is the exact McNemar $p$}{table.1}{}}
