\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Decision-level variants for the focused backbone (\textsc  {sensitiveai-vi-custom}) on the test split. Every variant reads the same frozen scores; only the mixing and decision rule differ. The last row is the paper's primary system. \emph  {Per-class columns are F1}; the best macro-F1 is in bold. The two rule-only rows are scored inside the fusion pipeline on the renormalised rule scores; the standalone rule engine, with its own thresholds, is reported in the text.}}{8}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:fusion-variants}{{2}{8}{Decision-level variants for the focused backbone (\model {sensitiveai-vi-custom}) on the test split. Every variant reads the same frozen scores; only the mixing and decision rule differ. The last row is the paper's primary system. \emph {Per-class columns are F1}; the best macro-F1 is in bold. The two rule-only rows are scored inside the fusion pipeline on the renormalised rule scores; the standalone rule engine, with its own thresholds, is reported in the text}{table.2}{}}
